  "described": {
    "alt_text": "The line art of the Cliffs of Volcano Ball Lake commission, inverted to thin white lines on solid black, showing a dense valley of huts, creatures, cliffs and a lake.",
    "description": "A square image of white line drawing on a black ground, with no colour or fill. It is the outline layer of the 2021 commission: a lake in the upper middle under rolling clouds, a striped volcano with a ball on its summit at upper right, cliffs and a winding river descending to a small city in the centre, rows of domed huts on a plateau at right, and a foreground crowded with horned and eyed creatures, stalks and blobs. Every contour is the same thin white weight, so the density of the original reads as a fine lace.",
    "impression": "The commission with its colour stripped away, like an X-ray of the drawing. Without fills it becomes a map of every decision the line made, and the crowding feels more like texture than population. It is a working file, made to be fed to a machine, and it is also quietly beautiful on its own.",
